    "b-sks-rc-tactics-intro": {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "TACTIC — A global table: a reusable move for turning a mismatch into a match. A "
        },
        {
          "insert": "tactic",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " row is not per target, and an attempt is not a tactic: a tactic is the idea (reorder two stores, inline the guard, hoist the load), and an attempt uses one or mints a new one. A row says when it applies ("
        },
        {
          "insert": "when",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": a precondition on what the diff, mismatch, or situation looks like), what to do ("
        },
        {
          "insert": "do",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": the steps, in the worker's terms), and where it was first minted ("
        },
        {
          "insert": "origin_attempt_id",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "). The patterns it resolves are "
        },
        {
          "insert": "pattern_tactic",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " rows. Every attempt that has used it is a "
        },
        {
          "insert": "tactic_use",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " row with an "
        },
        {
          "insert": "outcome",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", and "
        },
        {
          "insert": "success_rate",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " is derived from those rows by query, never stored. It is searchable across all targets: \"which tactics have a "
        },
        {
          "insert": "when",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " that looks like my current diff?\" Like "
        },
        {
          "insert": "knowledge_record",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " it is revisioned: a new row names the previous one in "
        },
        {
          "insert": "supersedes_id",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "."
        }
      ],
      "id": "b-sks-rc-tactics-intro",
      "children": []
    },
